<title>BELGIUM: EU sets unchanged 1997/98 milk, butter prices.</title>
<headline>EU sets unchanged 1997/98 milk, butter prices.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union milk, butter and skimmed milk prices will remain unchanged in 1997/98 (July/June), the EU said in a statement.</p>
<p>As part of the farm price package agreed in Luxembourg on Wednesday, the target price for milk stays at 309.8 Ecus per tonne and intervention prices for butter and skimmed milk powder at 3,282 and 2,055.2 Ecus per tonne respectively</p>
<p>Finland and Sweden's exemptions on milk fat content were extended for two years until December 31, 1999.</p>
<p>The European Commission was requested to propose a two year extension of special measures for east German states if no solution could be found for their milk quota problems.</p>
<p>The Commission was also asked to consider more flexible milk quota measures for Italian and Spanish producers.</p>
<p>-Brussels bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
